{
  "_help": "Basic attack skills (scripts/Attacks.cs, menu: O or Skills > Basic attacks). Each weapon class has one, used by the attack button whenever that class is equipped. The player builds its chain from unlocked steps (light attacks run the chain in order, then start over) and sockets modifiers into it, like supports on spells. Unlocking steps and modifiers and ranking up costs skill points (the same points as spells). Steps: base = which of the weapon's combo swings (data/weapons.json) to borrow timing and hand poses from, 'power' for the power attack; then any of dmg (x weapon damage), arc, range, knock, stun, up, lunge, spin, critBonus, finisher, speed (x attack speed), stamina (x cost), status {id: chance}, and for ranged classes shots, spread (degrees), pierce, aoe (m). The 'start' steps are free and form the first chain.",
  "maxRank": 5,
  "rankDmgP": 8,
  "chainByRank": [3, 4, 5, 6, 7],
  "socketsByRank": [1, 1, 2, 2, 3],
  "_animHelp": "anim = the attack animation a step plays (data/avatar.json \"attackAnims\"); powerAnim = the power attack's. rec (optional, per step) = the follow-through animation during its recovery.",
  "critical": { "_help": "Dark Souls pass: the animation of a critical blow (riposte after a parry, backstab), an attackAnims id in data/avatar.json; multipliers and ranges in data/tuning.json game.parry / game.backstab.", "anim": "riposte" },
  "_activeHelp": "Any step (and any combo / power attack in data/weapons.json) may set \"active\": [start, end], the fractions of the swing in which its hitbox is live (default: hit -0.1 .. hit +0.12, data/tuning.json game.hitbox), and \"step\": metres the swing carries the body forward (default by type, game.attack.step*).",
  "recovery": {
	"_recByAnimHelp": "recByAnim: the follow-through for one-handed steps by their animation (a step's own rec wins): Sword_Regular_B's own _Rec after the return cut.", "recByAnim": {}, "_animetool": "2026-11-27 AnimeTool: the light follow-through clips (Sword_Regular_A_Rec / B_Rec) swung the blade up to vertical with a 150-250 deg snap at the hand-over (and recA followed the thrust too), so light swings now blend straight into the guard (recLight empty; it was recA, recByAnim slashB was recB).",
	"_help": "Weight: seconds after a swing before the next one can start (you can still move, roll or block). light = ordinary chain steps, finisher = the chain's finisher steps, power = power (heavy) attacks. twoHandedMul / daggerMul / rangedMul scale it for those weapons. Faster attack speed shortens it. A step can set its own \"recover\". recLight / recHeavy: follow-through animations for one- and two-handed weapons.",
	"_a03": "A-03 (weight): light 0.05 -> 0.28, finisher 0.32 -> 0.5, power 0.5 -> 0.7; twoHandedMul 1.6 -> 1.4, daggerMul 0.5 -> 0.6 (rangedMul 0.6 kept). The swing itself is lengthened in data/tuning.json game.attack.",
	"light": 0.28, "finisher": 0.5, "power": 0.7,
	"twoHandedMul": 1.4, "daggerMul": 0.6, "rangedMul": 0.6,
	"recLight": "", "recHeavy": "recHook"
  },
